SUMMARY:Deadline: The Strong National Museum of Play: Research Fellowships\
 , January to May 2027 cycle (video game history and play\; USD 750/week)
DESCRIPTION:Short research residencies for work with The Strong's collectio
 ns: the Brian Sutton-Smith Library and Archives of Play\, the museum's art
 ifacts\, and the ICHEG electronic and video game holdings. The Strong and 
 Valentine/Cosman fellowships explicitly cover video and electronic games\,
  making this a digital-heritage and games-as-culture fit.\n\nOrganisation:
  The Strong National Museum of Play (incl. ICHEG\, International Center fo
 r the History of Electronic Games)\nLocation: Rochester\, New York\, USA. 
 In person\, full time. Applicants must live more than 50 miles from The St
 rong.\nAward: USD 750 per week for up to 4 weeks (Strong and Valentine/Cos
 man fellowships)\; G. Rollie Adams USD 750/week for up to 3 weeks\; France
 s M. Williams USD 750 flat. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to 4 weeks b
 etween January and May 2027\n\nMore: https://www.museumofplay.org/collecti
 ons/research-fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://www.museumofplay.org/collections/research-fellowships/?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rochester\, New York\, USA. In person\, full time. Applicants must
  live more than 50 miles from The Strong.
END:VEVENT
